{{Infobox treaty|name=Mutual Arms and Technology Agreement|long_name=|image=Signing of Mutual Arms and Technology Agreement.jpg|image_width=280px|caption=Signing of MATA in Kyiv|type=|date_drafted=|date_signed={{Start date|1977|08|10|df=y}}|location_signed={{W|Kyiv}}, [[Ukraine]]|date_sealed=|date_effective=|condition_effective=|date_expiration=|signatories={{flagicon|Balisca}} [[Mário Sá Justino]]<br> {{flagicon|Philippines}} [[Stuart Aquino]] <br> {{flagicon|Sanyan}} [[Fumnanya Yobachukwu]] <br> {{flagicon|Soviet Union}} [[tba]]|parties={{flag|Balisca}} <br> {{flag|Philippines}} <br> {{flag|Sanyan}} <br> {{flag|Soviet Union}}|depositor=|citations=|languages=[[Baliscano language|Baliscano]], {{W|Filipino language|Filipino}}, [[Kinza language|Kinza]] and {{W|Russian language|Russian}}|wikisource=}}The '''Mutual Arms and Technology Agreement''' ('''MATA'''; {{Lang-bl|Acuerdo Mutual d’Armas y Tecnología}}; '''AMAT;''' an apronym meaning "beloved") is a defense cooperation agreement between [[Balisca]], the [[Philippines]], [[Sanyan]] and the [[Soviet Union]]. It was signed in the aftermath of the [[South Atlantic War]] and [[Gulf of Guinea Crisis]], after which Balisca abandoned it's longstanding confederal policy of [[W:Armed neutrality|armed neutrality]].

The pact includes cooperation on advanced {{W|cyberwarfare}}, {{W|artificial intelligence}} and autonomy, {{W|quantum technologies}}, {{W|undersea capabilities}}, {{W|Hypersonic weapon|hypersonic and counter-hypersonic weapons}}, {{W|electronic warfare}}, innovation and {{W|Intelligence sharing|information sharing}}.
